   1 #!/usr/bin/env python3
   2 """Restart-resilient supervisor for external model lanes on macOS.
   3 
   4 This tool is deliberately a wrapper around, not a replacement for,
   5 ``ops/lane.sh``.  The existing launcher remains the sole writer of the
   6 schema-2 run receipt and retains all prompt, sandbox, and hash custody.
   7 
   8 The wrapper loads ``lane.sh`` as a one-shot per-user launchd job.  The job is
   9 therefore outside the coordinator/terminal process tree and survives an
  10 accidental Codex-process termination.  While a job is live, ``status`` and
  11 ``wait`` consult only launchd plus ``.lane-jobs/<tag>/launch.v1.json``; they
  12 never open the active report, model log, or ``.run.v2`` receipt.  Once launchd
  13 reports a terminal state, the coordinator must still follow receipt-first
  14 custody before reading any report or log.
  15 
  16 Usage::
  17 
  18     python3 ops/lane_detach.py launch ADAPTER TAG PROMPT
  19     python3 ops/lane_detach.py status TAG [--json]
  20     python3 ops/lane_detach.py wait TAG [--timeout SECONDS] [--json]
  21     python3 ops/lane_detach.py list [--json | --running-tags]
  22     python3 ops/lane_detach.py unload TAG
  23 
  24 ``unload`` refuses a live job.  It removes only the terminal launchd
  25 registration and keeps the ignored sidecar as crash-recovery history.
  26 """
  27 
  28 from __future__ import annotations
